        "id": 2016993
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-24T14:14:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the first loop it restarts probing the services who are being probed. In the second loop it restarts announcing the services whose probing have been finished. I don\u0027t see a chance that a service can finish re-probing before the second loop. \nThus I think these two loops shouldn\u0027t process any service in common. \n\nIs there a race condition example you can think of?",
